ost, a Ryzen 9 7900X3D system with 64 GB DDR5 and an Intel Arc A770 16 GB GPU, running Arch Linux and KDE Plasma 6.\n* The session involved multiple kernel versions, starting with `7.3.0-rc1-273-tkg-bore` and later switching to `7.3.0-rc5-273-linux73-tkg-bore-rc5-xe` to bind the A770 GPU to the `xe` driver.\n* The session included various technical analyses, consolidated benchmark results, and an issues ledger, which are documented in sections 4-6 of the notes.\n* The session also involved testing oneAPI 2026.1 and oneDNN A/B, as well as investigating a DG2 XMX-gather IGC crash patch and 256-GRF kernels.\n* The session was conducted in two contexts: Context A, which ran from September 26 to 28, and Context B, which resumed on October 1.\n* The session notes include a chronological record of 15 phases, as well as a glossary and evidence inventory.\n* The session was requested to be thoroughly documented, and the notes include a detailed record of the session, including timestamps, commands, and output."}